  "calibration": "Calibration: recent tasks under these rules and how often the reference agent solved them (target: 1-3 of 5 runs).\nPer kind: judgement/property_completeness: 1 task(s), 3/5\n- http-header-crlf-injection-audit [property_completeness]: 3/5 -> learnable (The task split 3/2 pass/fail because of a critical ambiguity: the instructions didn't clearly specify that CRLF must be stripped/sanitized rather than rejected with 400 errors, so one failing agent rejected requests entirely (breaking test_redirect_no_crlf, test_request_id_no_crlf) while another's sanitization crashed the server (breaking test_clean_redirect_still_works and others). All passing runs correctly stripped CRLF while preserving normal HTTP functionality across redirect, cookie, request-id, and display-name paths. Next design should add an explicit rule distinguishing 'sanitize by stripping' from 'reject with error' and keep the dual-property structure (security + functionality) since the mutation check killed all 5 faults.). Fix all CRLF injection vulnerabilities across a small URL-shortener HTTP service that sets headers through varied code paths and abstraction layers.\nTasks solved too often had few rules, rules on one theme, or an oracle to compare against. Make this design harder with more independent, precisely stated rules on more themes and sharper hidden inputs; never by hiding rules. Make it easier than the too_hard ones.",
